					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12349498#post-4343388</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12349498/roadside-cafe#post-4343388</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 29 Aug 2019 03:39:43 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Marina Hayes</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4526632</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This was certainly engaging. Especially the descriptions of eating, they actually made me a little squeemish.<br /> I only have two minor nitpicks.</p> <p>Having a person remind the OP to bring their phone to take some pictures, only for the OP to <em>not</em> do so feels like an odd choice. It almost feels like that one comment could just be removed, but I can see the value in having a slightly-too-eager word of encouragment from crilasxowe.</p> <p>My other nitpick is suuuper minor, but the OP's description of the voice in the basement, specifically the &quot;such desparation, such agony&quot; part feels a bit over-dramatic, but that could just be me.</p> <p>Still, +1 from me</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
